<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:section xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="62413" href="schedule/2015/spring/CWL/199/62413.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2015" href="schedule/2015.xml">2015</calendarYear><term id="120151" href="schedule/2015/spring.xml">Spring 2015</term><subject id="CWL" href="schedule/2015/spring/CWL.xml">Comparative and World Literature</subject><course id="199" href="schedule/2015/spring/CWL/199.xml">Undergraduate Open Seminar</course></parents><sectionNumber>A  </sectionNumber><sectionTitle>The Human Experience</sectionTitle><creditHours>3 hours</creditHours><statusCode>A</statusCode><sectionText>Topic:  The Human Experience: Language, Identity, Memory &amp; Diaspora.  This interdisciplinary course approaches the study of global cultures through literature-in-translation and film. Organized thematically into four units, Language, Identity, Memory and Diaspora, the format of the course is creative and participatory. Chronologically the course reaches from the archaic origins of language into the present day; geographically the course traverses the globe.</sectionText><partOfTerm>1</partOfTerm><sectionStatusCode>A</sectionStatusCode><enrollmentStatus>CrossListOpen</enrollmentStatus><startDate>2015-01-20Z</startDate><endDate>2015-05-06Z</endDate><meetings><meeting id="0"><type code="LCD">Lecture-Discussion</type><start>11:00 AM</start><end>12:20 PM</end><daysOfTheWeek>TR     </daysOfTheWeek><roomNumber>170</roomNumber><buildingName>Wohlers Hall</buildingName><instructors><instructor lastName="Pintar" firstName="J">Pintar, J</instructor></instructors></meeting></meetings></ns2:section>